        <obo:IAO_0000115>A village biome is an anthropogenic terrestrial biome which contains settlements such as villages, towns, and/or small cities and which is primarily used for agricultural activity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>ORCID:0000-0002-4366-3088</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2013-06-14T11:45:47Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <rdfs:comment>Villages are also described as agricultural settlements with greater than 100 persons per square kilometre; however, no upper limit is defined.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>village biome</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000246"/>
