        <owl:annotatedTarget>The process of shaping a trabecula in the heart. A trabecula is a small, often microscopic, tissue element in the form of a small beam, strut or rod, which generally has a mechanical function. Trabecula are usually but not necessarily, composed of dense collagenous tissue.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GOC:dph</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


