        <obo:IAO_0000115>A neuromuscular junction in which the target muscle cell is a myotube.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>dos</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2013-10-14T12:05:12Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>cellular_component</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>GO:0098523</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>In vertebrates, the term &apos;neuromuscular junction&apos; is limited to synapses targeting the myotubes of skeletal muscle (AKA skeletal muscle fibers). Neuromuscular junctions targeting other muscle cell types exist in invertebrates such as the mononucleate somatic muscles of nematodes.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>neuromuscular junction of myotube</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
