        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9369"/>
        <oboInOwl:notes>most adult placentals have no trace of a cloaca. However, the tenrecs and golden moles, small placental mammals native to Africa, retain a cloaca as adults.</oboInOwl:notes>
