        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cardiac atrium that is in the right side of the heart. It receives deoxygenated blood. In mammals, this comes from the superior and inferior vena cava and the coronary sinus, and pumps it into the right ventricle through the tricuspid valve.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:RO_0002175 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>Right cardiac chamber which is continuous with the superior vena cava and inferior vena cava.[FMA]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>The tetrapod clade develops a complete atrial septum and loses the fifth aortic arch altogether.[well established][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000006 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/wiki/Modeling-paired-structures-Design-Pattern</obo:UBPROP_0000006>
