        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>An arterial trunk with origin from the right ventricle of the heart, and dividing into the right and left pulmonary arteries, which enter the corresponding lungs and branch with the bronchi. [TFD][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>As in birds, the conus arteriosus split during embryonic development in mammals to produce the pulmonary trunk and single aortic trunk of the adult.[well established][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
