        <owl:annotatedTarget>An illuminance unit which is equal to the illuminance produced by 1 lumen evenly spread over an area 1 m^[2].</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NIST:NIST</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000118">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A luminous flux unit which is equal to the luminous flux emitted into 1 steradian by a point source of 1 candela.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>lm</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>&quot;A luminous flux unit which is equal to the luminous flux emitted into 1 steradian by a point source of 1 candela.&quot; [NIST:NIST]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>lumen</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000118"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A luminous flux unit which is equal to the luminous flux emitted into 1 steradian by a point source of 1 candela.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NIST:NIST</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000120">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A catalytic unit activity which is equal to the activity of a catalyst in moles per second, such as the amount of an enzyme needed to transform one mole of substrate per second.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>kat</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>&quot;A catalytic unit activity which is equal to the activity of a catalyst in moles per second, such as the amount of an enzyme needed to transform one mole of substrate per second.&quot; [NIST:NIST]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>katal</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000120"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A catalytic unit activity which is equal to the activity of a catalyst in moles per second, such as the amount of an enzyme needed to transform one mole of substrate per second.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NIST:NIST</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000123">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A plane angle unit which is equal to the angle subtended at the center of a circle by an arc equal in length to the radius of the circle, approximately 57 degrees 17 minutes and 44.6 seconds.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>rad</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>&quot;A plane angle unit which is equal to the angle subtended at the center of a circle by an arc equal in length to the radius of the circle, approximately 57 degrees 17 minutes and 44.6 seconds.&quot; [NIST:NIST]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>radian</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000123"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A plane angle unit which is equal to the angle subtended at the center of a circle by an arc equal in length to the radius of the circle, approximately 57 degrees 17 minutes and 44.6 seconds.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NIST:NIST</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000125">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A solid angle unit which is equal to the solid angle subtended at the center of a sphere by an area on the surface of the sphere that is equal to the radius squared.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>sr</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>&quot;A solid angle unit which is equal to the solid angle subtended at the center of a sphere by an area on the surface of the sphere that is equal to the radius squared.&quot; [NIST:NIST]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>steradian</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000125"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A solid angle unit which is equal to the solid angle subtended at the center of a sphere by an area on the surface of the sphere that is equal to the radius squared.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NIST:NIST</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000132">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An activity (of a radionuclide) unit which is equal to the activity of a quantity of radioactive material in which one nucleus decays per second or there is one atom disintegration per second (dps).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Bq</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>&quot;An activity (of a radionuclide) unit which is equal to the activity of a quantity of radioactive material in which one nucleus decays per second or there is one atom disintegration per second (dps).&quot; [NIST:NIST]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>becquerel</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000132"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An activity (of a radionuclide) unit which is equal to the activity of a quantity of radioactive material in which one nucleus decays per second or there is one atom disintegration per second (dps).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NIST:NIST</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000133">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An activity (of a radionuclide) unit which is equal to the activity of a quantity of radioactive material in which there are 3.7 x 10^[10] atom disintegration per second (dps).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Ci</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>&quot;An activity (of a radionuclide) unit which is equal to the activity of a quantity of radioactive material in which there are 3.7 x 10^[10] atom disintegration per second (dps).&quot; [ORCBS:ORCBS]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>curie</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An activity (of a radionuclide) unit which is equal to the activity of a quantity of radioactive material in which there are 3.7 x 10^[10] atom disintegration per second (dps).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ORCBS:ORCBS</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000134">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An absorbed dose unit which is equal to the absorption of one joule of radiation energy by one kilogram of matter.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Gy</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>&quot;An absorbed dose unit which is equal to the absorption of one joule of radiation energy by one kilogram of matter.&quot; [NIST:NIST]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>gray</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000134"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An absorbed dose unit which is equal to the absorption of one joule of radiation energy by one kilogram of matter.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NIST:NIST</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000135">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An absorbed dose unit which is equal to 0.01 gray (Gy).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>&quot;An absorbed dose unit which is equal to 0.01 gray (Gy).&quot; [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>rad</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000135"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An absorbed dose unit which is equal to 0.01 gray (Gy).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Wikipedia</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000136">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An exposure unit which is equal to the amount of radiation required to liberate positive and negative charges of one electrostatic unit of charge in 1 cm^[3] of air at standard temperature and pressure (STP). This corresponds to the generation of approximately 2.0810^[9] ion pairs.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>R</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>&quot;An exposure unit which is equal to the amount of radiation required to liberate positive and negative charges of one electrostatic unit of charge in 1 cm^[3] of air at standard temperature and pressure (STP). This corresponds to the generation of approximately 2.0810^[9] ion pairs.&quot; [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>roentgen</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000136"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An exposure unit which is equal to the amount of radiation required to liberate positive and negative charges of one electrostatic unit of charge in 1 cm^[3] of air at standard temperature and pressure (STP). This corresponds to the generation of approximately 2.0810^[9] ion pairs.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Wikipedia</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000137">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A dose equivalent unit which is equal to the absorption of one joule of radiation energy by one kilogram of matter.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Sv</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>&quot;A dose equivalent unit which is equal to the absorption of one joule of radiation energy by one kilogram of matter.&quot; [NIST:NIST]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>sievert</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000137"/>
